  "info": {
    "description": "\nRead-only bowling ball data for BowlerIQ partner platforms: specs per weight,\ncover and core, ball motion plotter positions with suggestions, and links to\nBowlerDepot Learn reviews and BowlerDepot product pages.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. **Get a key.** BowlerIQ issues one key per partner platform. Keep it\n   server-side: never ship it in a browser or mobile app.\n2. **Send it on every request** as `Authorization: Bearer <your key>`.\n   To try calls on this page, click **Authentication** and paste your key;\n   it's sent only to `api.bowleriq.io`.\n3. **Load everything once**, then **keep in sync** with `GET /v1/changes`\n   (see *Syncing* below).\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BOWLERIQ_PARTNER_KEY\" \\\n  \"https://api.bowleriq.io/partner/v1/changes?limit=50\"\n```\n\n## Basics\n\n- **Format:** JSON. Every response includes `\"api_version\": \"1\"`.\n- **Rate limit:** about 10 requests/second, bursts of 20. Over that you get\n  `429`; back off and retry.\n- **Paging:** `limit` defaults to 200, maximum 500. Follow `next_cursor`.\n- **Ids** are stable UUIDs; use them as your keys. Each colorway is its own ball.\n\n## The v1 promise\n\nv1 only **grows**: we may add optional fields and new endpoints, so ignore\nfields you don't recognise. Within v1 we will never rename or remove a field\nor endpoint, change a field's type, units or meaning, or make an optional\nfield required. Any of those ships as `/v2`, and `/v1` keeps running while\nyou migrate.\n\n## Syncing\n\n```text\ncursor = load_saved_cursor()                    # None on the very first run\nloop:\n    page = GET /v1/changes?cursor=<cursor>      # omit cursor the first time\n    for change in page.items:\n        if change.change == \"upsert\": save(change.ball)   # create/replace by id\n        if change.change == \"remove\": delete(change.id)\n    cursor = page.next_cursor\n    save_cursor(cursor)                         # after applying the page\n    if not page.has_more: break\n```\n\n- Run it every 15-60 minutes. The **first run** returns every published ball\n  as an `upsert`; to start from a point in time pass `?since=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z`.\n- **Always store `next_cursor`** and send it next time. Don't use the time of\n  your last run as `since`: that can skip changes.\n- Re-running from your last saved cursor is safe; upserts and removes can be\n  applied more than once.\n- A ball appears once per page with its latest state. Changes appear about\n  60 seconds after they happen.\n- A ball counts as changed when its own fields, any weight's specs, its\n  images or its Learn review link change.\n\n## Errors\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `400` | Bad `cursor` or `since`. Restart from your last good cursor. |\n| `401` / `403` | Missing or invalid key |\n| `404` | Ball not found or not published |\n| `429` | Rate limited; retry with backoff |\n| `5xx` | Our problem; retry with backoff |\n",
    "summary": "Read-only bowling ball data for BowlerIQ partner platforms.",
    "title": "BowlerIQ Partner API",
    "version": "1"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/v1/balls": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Every published ball, current and retired. Good for a one-time full load; use /v1/changes to stay in sync.",
        "operationId": "get_balls_v1_balls_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "next_cursor from the previous page.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "cursor",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "next_cursor from the previous page.",
              "title": "Cursor"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 200,
              "maximum": 500,
              "minimum": 1,
              "title": "Limit",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BallPage"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "400": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorDetail"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Bad cursor or since."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GatewayError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Missing key."
          },
          "403": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GatewayError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Invalid key."
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GatewayError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Rate limited; retry with backoff."
          }
        },
        "summary": "All published balls (full load), paged by id",
        "tags": [
          "Balls"
        ]
      }
    },
